<http://dbpedia.org/resource/1920_TCU_Horned_Frogs_football_team> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/isPrimaryTopicOf> <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1920_TCU_Horned_Frogs_football_team> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/1920_TCU_Horned_Frogs_football_team> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The 1920 TCU Horned Frogs football team represented Texas Christian University (TCU) as a member of the Texas Intercollegiate Athletic Association (TIAA) during the 1920 college football season. Led by first-year head coach William L. Driver, the Frogs compiled an overall record of 9–1 with a conference mark of 3–0, winning the TIAA title. TCU hosted Centre on New Year's Day in the Fort Worth Classic, losing by a score of 63 to 7. The team's captain was Astyanax Douglass, who played center."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/1920_TCU_Horned_Frogs_football_team> <http://dbpedia.org/property/stadium> "Clarke Field, Panther Park"@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/1920_TCU_Horned_Frogs_football_team> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/abstract> "The 1920 TCU Horned Frogs football team represented Texas Christian University (TCU) as a member of the Texas Intercollegiate Athletic Association (TIAA) during the 1920 college football season. Led by first-year head coach William L. Driver, the Frogs compiled an overall record of 9–1 with a conference mark of 3–0, winning the TIAA title. TCU hosted Centre on New Year's Day in the Fort Worth Classic, losing by a score of 63 to 7. The team's captain was Astyanax Douglass, who played center."@en .
