<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Drag_cost> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Drag cost is a project management metric developed by Stephen Devaux as part of the Total Project Control (TPC) approach to project schedule and cost analysis. It is the amount by which a project’s expected return on investment (ROI) is reduced due to the critical path drag of a specific critical path activity Task (project management) or other specific schedule factor such as a schedule lag or other delaying constraint. Drag cost is computed at the activity level, but is caused by the impact at the project level due to:"@en .
