<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cost_contingency> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "或有事項（英語：Contingency）是一個會計學的概念，通常是指企業在會計核算中經常面臨某些不確定情形，需要會計人員作出分析和判斷，並根據重大程度決定是否在會計報表中反映。有些情形下，其最終結果須以未來事件的發生或不發生來加以證實。常見的或有事項包括:商業票據貼現、未決訴訟、產品質量保證、貸款保證等。"@zh .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cost_contingency> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "When estimating the cost for a project, product or other item or investment, there is always uncertainty as to the precise content of all items in the estimate, how work will be performed, what work conditions will be like when the project is executed and so on. These uncertainties are risks to the project. Some refer to these risks as \"known-unknowns\" because the estimator is aware of them, and based on past experience, can even estimate their probable costs. The estimated costs of the known-unknowns is referred to by cost estimators as cost contingency."@en .
