<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Gregory_Duralev> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/abstract> "Abstract of the information: Gregory Duralev (born in Barnaul, Altai Krai, Russia) is a former Russian bodybuilder, businessman, and Russian economist who fled his home country in 2015 after writing his civil initiative on Strategy to develop the Russian economy by supporting medium and small business and comprehensive program to fight against corruption and uploading it directly to the website of the President of Russia V.V. Putin. Subsequently, Gregory Duralev being charged with fraud under fabricated allegations. Arriving in the United States, he filed for political asylum on January 25, 2016 and was permitted by the Department of Homeland Security to remain in the United States until his application would be decided. However, in September 2018, while awaiting the decision of his asylum application, he was arrested by the subdevision of the Department of Homeland Security - Immigration and Customs Enforcement in Los Angeles on the charge of remaining in the United States without permission notwithstanding that the permission allowing Gregory Duralev to remain in the United States as an asylum seeker was still valid. As it turned out later, the official documents signed by the employees of the Department of Homeland Security revealed, the real reason of the conducted arrest was because he was the subject of the INTERPOL Red Notice from Russia even though it was outside of the official power given to the Department of Homeland Security by the legislation of the United States. Gregory Duralev was sent to a maximum security prison from where he was relocated several times to the different immigration facilities in California. Until early 2020 he was released on Immigration bond Gregory Duralev had been detained for approximately 525 days in the United States for administrative violation that he had never committed. After he was released Gregory Duralev applied and was admitted to the Washington University in St. Louis School of Law (WashULaw). Gregory Duralev is still pursuing his immigration case along with his legal fight for reinstatement of his right that should have secured but violated by the United States having undertaken the important international legal obligation before the United Nations under Refugee Act of 1980 and Protocol Relating to the Status of Refugees."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Gregory_Duralev> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Gregory Duralev"@en .
