<http://dbpedia.org/resource/List_of_subdivisions_of_County_Dublin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "County Dublin refers to a subdivision of Ireland occasioned by the Norman invasion of Ireland. This shire or county underwent further subdivisions as the territory was subinfeudated by the great barons among their vassals; these smaller areas were known as baronies. Under the government of the Kingdom of Ireland, baronies were in turn split into civil parishes. These also were split into the lowest recognised legal unit of land - the townland."@en .
