<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Laverna_Katie_Dollimore> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Laverna \"Verna\" Katie Dollimore OC (January 22, 1922 – October 24, 2011) was one of six Canadians awarded the Order of Canada for her participation in the Canadian Caper, in which the Canadian government and the CIA orchestrated the cover rescue of six American diplomats in Iran (1979). Her Order of Canada Medal is on display at the Maritime Command Museum. She joined the International Commission for Supervision and Control, under in Laos in 1969. For her services there she received the Canadian Peacekeeping Service Medal."@en .
