<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Swayne,_Robinson_and_Company> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Swayne, Robinson and Company also known as \"Swayne, Robinson & Co.\" or simple \"Swayne, Robinson\" was an iron and aluminum casting factory founded in 1842 by Francis W. Robinson. The company operated until 1997, when it closed and its owners filed for bankruptcy. The building was located at 214 East Main Street Richmond, Indiana until 2001. A fire in 1999 destroyed a third of the building. It is the current site of the Wayne County Jail. Until it closed, it was the oldest family-owned business in America."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Swayne,_Robinson_and_Company> <http://dbpedia.org/property/keyPeople> "Samuel Swayne, Secretary , President"@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Swayne,_Robinson_and_Company> <http://dbpedia.org/property/keyPeople> "Charles K. Robinson, President"@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Swayne,_Robinson_and_Company> <http://dbpedia.org/property/keyPeople> "Henry Robinson, President"@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Swayne,_Robinson_and_Company> <http://dbpedia.org/property/keyPeople> "Francis W. Robinson , President"@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Swayne,_Robinson_and_Company> <http://dbpedia.org/property/keyPeople> "Henry R. Robinson, President"@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Swayne,_Robinson_and_Company> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/abstract> "Swayne, Robinson and Company also known as \"Swayne, Robinson & Co.\" or simple \"Swayne, Robinson\" was an iron and aluminum casting factory founded in 1842 by Francis W. Robinson. The company operated until 1997, when it closed and its owners filed for bankruptcy. The building was located at 214 East Main Street Richmond, Indiana until 2001. A fire in 1999 destroyed a third of the building. It is the current site of the Wayne County Jail. Until it closed, it was the oldest family-owned business in America."@en .
