<http://dbpedia.org/resource/William_Mitchel_Daily> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "William Mitchel Daily (1812–February 5, 1877) was an American academic, preacher and theologian. He served as the third president of Indiana University and resigned under pressure after fewer than six years. He served a one-year term as the chaplain of the US House of Representatives and also served as a hospital chaplain during the US Civil War."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/William_Mitchel_Daily> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/abstract> "William Mitchel Daily (1812–February 5, 1877) was an American academic, preacher and theologian. He served as the third president of Indiana University and resigned under pressure after fewer than six years. He served a one-year term as the chaplain of the US House of Representatives and also served as a hospital chaplain during the US Civil War."@en .
